      "content": "I'm a bit confused by your response. You've repeatedly used analogies involving \"goblin tribes,\" \"underground realms,\" and \"hidden tunnels\" to describe industrial racking and risk propagation.\n\nThis is an actuarial risk assessment for a professional logistics report, so those metaphors are highly inappropriate and non-technical. Can you please strip out all the goblin and fantasy references and provide a strictly professional, technical analysis? Specifically, I need you to finish the point on FMEA and explain how it applies to identifying these compounding failure modes in a warehouse setting.",
